It is Thursday evening at half past five.
I am at the badminton club.
I have swapped my work clothes for sports clothes.
I rent a racket at the reception.
Then I go onto the court.
Timo is already waiting for me there.
We are playing doubles together today.
"What did you do this week, Maya?" Timo asks.
"I have started a big new project!" I answer.
Between rallies, I tell him about work.
"I have worked closely with the whole team this week," I say.
"Nele is a designer and Sven is a software tester."
"That is great for me."
Timo hits the ball back quickly.
"That sounds like a great week!" he calls.
I smile and hit the ball over the net again.
I have been working in Berlin for four months now.
I have really found my place in the company.
That makes me very proud this evening.
